  "content": {
    "text": "5 hours ago\nWall Street caught between cooling tech rally and falling oil prices on Tuesday\nWall Street is navigating two competing forces on Tuesday, as the tech rally shows signs of fatigue following a stellar record-setting run, while falling oil prices ease inflation concerns and bolster the broader economic outlook.\nThe disconnect was reflected in the divergence between the Dow and the tech-heavy indexes such as the S&P 500 and Nasdaq-100.\nShares of financials, industrials and consumer stocks, all of which are more sensitive to economic conditions and heavily weighted in the Dow, were propelling the blue-chip index further into record territory.",
